#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115393 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114973 :question/id #uuid "228ae66f-9dad-5e6d-b405-9fbe62ecb7e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2480" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{t}^{2}\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{t}\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\\\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\\\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\\\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048954 :topic/id #uuid "cee13705-0b60-5ea0-b11e-46fd35bede4e" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059731}] :topic/math-academy-id 177 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048233} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048297} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048377} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049291} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049436} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049663} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049814} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049853} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050336} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825}] :topic/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using Components"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186730326 :question-generator/id #uuid "74f4688f-6802-5a2e-b7c0-1496b5f67f27" :question-generator/script "generators/70/70673b4ec3611e784bb88a73d3307818eea20da4464a4cd393ccd8331938468b/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0582802c-da60-55c8-b827-54e85f4c84ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+11{t}^{2}+12t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299957} {:answer/id #uuid "1b314b6c-c07c-5dd1-84b0-ae7405c80fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300087} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffe098b-3d9f-5f11-993f-cab4cc8b011e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+14t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300454} {:answer/id #uuid "923e3fa5-b372-5604-81b4-5c6bf37d1887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300695} {:answer/id #uuid "e3888121-e3fe-55f8-8939-41b8db9b90ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3888121-e3fe-55f8-8939-41b8db9b90ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301095} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2898930-3fb5-5dee-8009-dea699857dae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301942}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a209f44d-4003-53ab-9d12-642d62514eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32298" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =20t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(2+5t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & ={t}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+({t}^{2}+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =20\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+5\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}+(2t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t) & ={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+5\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+({t}^{2}+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})+(20t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(2+5t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}+(2t+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564ab4d2-73e6-558b-9af0-6f5fdd10eee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21t+10 \\\\ 45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390745} {:answer/id #uuid "08d9d97e-52f1-593e-bf6d-177ead5a4e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ 42t+20 \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390746} {:answer/id #uuid "20623cb8-9b6d-552a-a5b9-c2b26e55fa4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-42t-20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ 24{t}^{3}+2t+6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390747} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a88e03-753f-57ff-a632-12697f009654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-24{t}^{3}-2t-6 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ 42t+20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390748} {:answer/id #uuid "31d0af8e-650c-555d-ad59-94751914d534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d0af8e-650c-555d-ad59-94751914d534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390749} :answer-field/id #uuid "e189a085-a70a-5dfd-9709-316634fc8cbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390744}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54437c76-a800-5517-9d6f-6a2f64f033aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-32353" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3{t}^{2} \\\\ t+4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{g}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ -2{t}^{2} \\\\ 5t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6t \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4t \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 6t & 1 & 0 \\\\ t+2 & -2{t}^{2} & 5t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2{t}^{2} & 5t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}6t & 0 \\\\ t+2 & 5t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}6t & 1 \\\\ t+2 & -2{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5t \\\\ -30{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{f}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & t+4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4t & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}t+4 & 8 \\\\ -4t & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}3{t}^{2} & 8 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}3{t}^{2} & t+4 \\\\ 1 & -4t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}37t+20 \\\\ 8-15{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5t \\\\ -30{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}37t+20 \\\\ 8-15{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b93f617-87e0-5210-be19-97741891991d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260262} {:answer/id #uuid "3580541f-830f-598a-a783-88fec72dde5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260354} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a9d477-3e12-5007-82c2-dfea71222f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,t,\\,3t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261312} {:answer/id #uuid "af3b5194-5a5b-5ac7-8760-ba017f3228d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261421} {:answer/id #uuid "baf1879f-f001-552d-a8d4-7e78fda261e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3580541f-830f-598a-a783-88fec72dde5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260354} :answer-field/id #uuid "f56a291e-1a05-5ec8-8e7b-40a05867d66d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262550}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "995d1b63-3fd5-54e1-bbec-560efe7ac735" :question/math-academy-id "q-128586" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}$ given that  $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}t,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}t⟩$ and $v(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}=v(t){\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)+{v}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}t),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\hspace{0.167em}2t,\\hspace{0.167em}1⟩ \\\\ {v}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'} & =v(t){\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)+{v}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\hspace{0.167em}2t,\\hspace{0.167em}1⟩+2⟨\\operatorname{ln}t,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\hspace{0.167em}4{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}2t⟩+⟨2\\operatorname{ln}t,\\hspace{0.167em}2{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}2t⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨\\operatorname{ln}t+1,\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c405b6-8e2c-5767-9204-4bdb2fa66d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{3},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259956} {:answer/id #uuid "6e532cd0-5a24-5b51-bb5f-bc2c5bfaaba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260847} {:answer/id #uuid "6fce5174-2553-542e-83df-f8d10e69e544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{4},\\,3{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260856} {:answer/id #uuid "9d94ed22-c699-542a-beb8-1d79f82bd0b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{2},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261240} {:answer/id #uuid "bca4179f-3737-54cf-b42b-7f31dd9110b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca4179f-3737-54cf-b42b-7f31dd9110b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261540} :answer-field/id #uuid "74146d36-b0eb-5ca0-9527-75ddfa0fc7f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262318}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2c98f03-8eb1-5c14-ba1a-38fe2722976d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128587" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'}$ where $\\mathbf{g}(t)=⟨t,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}2{t}^{3}⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(u\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'}=u(t){\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)+{u}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{g}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.167em}2t,\\hspace{0.167em}6{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'} & =u(t){\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)+{u}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{g}(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}⟨1,\\hspace{0.167em}2t,\\hspace{0.167em}6{t}^{2}⟩+3{t}^{2}⟨t,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}2{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\hspace{0.167em}2{t}^{4},\\hspace{0.167em}6{t}^{5}⟩+⟨3{t}^{3},\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{4},\\hspace{0.167em}6{t}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\hspace{0.167em}5{t}^{4},\\hspace{0.167em}12{t}^{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2f0c39-14ec-595e-a4ae-3b0e0f36d00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{t+1},\\,2,\\,4{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260134} {:answer/id #uuid "37f837c5-b882-5c17-be53-31f9d462ba0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,-3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260372} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2ab197-ba6d-56ea-b802-ada707de7359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-2,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260980} {:answer/id #uuid "87cd4c98-ec33-54b2-a15c-b9f4c0dc1eed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261057} {:answer/id #uuid "b3735980-9110-5643-906a-122ec95305f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3735980-9110-5643-906a-122ec95305f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261458} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e222c03-3a8a-5590-9dfe-dfec486e1c04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262149}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d768288b-91a5-51ed-b29b-7650008bff18" :question/math-academy-id "q-128894" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}$ given that  $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨{e}^{t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}{e}^{-t},\\hspace{0.167em}{e}^{2t}⟩$ and $v(t)={e}^{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}=v(t){\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)+{v}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t+1}),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}-{e}^{-t},\\hspace{0.167em}2{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\ {v}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'} & =v(t){\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)+{v}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}-{e}^{-t},\\hspace{0.167em}2{e}^{2t}⟩+{e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}{e}^{-t},\\hspace{0.167em}{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}-1,\\hspace{0.167em}2{e}^{3t}⟩+⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}1,\\hspace{0.167em}{e}^{3t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\hspace{0.167em}0,\\hspace{0.167em}3{e}^{3t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa27233-ccd6-5600-aa83-1e26fdfc1d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300082} {:answer/id #uuid "4659858f-2f59-59af-8140-bdeb6a985b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300314} {:answer/id #uuid "4dbb3dee-7a8c-53dc-9b4d-450bf35eee82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300366} {:answer/id #uuid "847f2c4d-2f3a-5e6c-b901-f7b8090c71a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300621} {:answer/id #uuid "c35962a3-cffe-5d24-bfef-7b8c30272350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dbb3dee-7a8c-53dc-9b4d-450bf35eee82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300366} :answer-field/id #uuid "7edc08bf-eaa3-58b5-8650-9797f1b61df8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301622}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19486880-810b-5bd6-a22c-f282191bb018" :question/math-academy-id "q-32804" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{f}(t)=2{t}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(1+5{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$, find $({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(t)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+5{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+5\\cdot 2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+10t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ {\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(0)\\mathbf{j}+(10)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =12t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+10\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t) & ={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(t)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) \\\\  & =(12t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+10\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (2{t}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(1+5{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})+(6{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+10t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (6{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+10t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =(12t\\cdot 2{t}^{3}+0\\cdot (-2t)+10\\cdot (1+5{t}^{2}))+((6{t}^{2})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(10t)^{2}) \\\\  & =24{t}^{4}+0+10+50{t}^{2}+36{t}^{4}+4+100{t}^{2} \\\\  & =60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb30d24-e5fa-5ff3-b793-37ff771c864a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300014} {:answer/id #uuid "26a29261-3951-5f05-aa91-50190f871a3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300147} {:answer/id #uuid "54f4bc9d-9659-533f-bcde-0d8203d7cee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300401} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8ad0ce-f737-58e3-9a2a-e7e35fa2da52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300509} {:answer/id #uuid "849785f2-76ee-5ce4-8123-ab009fa163a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849785f2-76ee-5ce4-8123-ab009fa163a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300624} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d48190f-ac7f-5e0c-a042-b8a82e88e0a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301675}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38bbc30d-2715-5fd5-8cc3-adae49e8b272" :question/math-academy-id "q-32835" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{3}-1⟩$, find $({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write: \n\n$$({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(t)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}6t⟩\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t) & ={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(t)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}6t⟩\\cdot ⟨{t}^{2}-1\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{3}-1⟩+⟨2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =(2\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1)+0\\cdot (2t)+6t\\cdot ({t}^{3}-1))+((2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(3{t}^{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2+0+6{t}^{4}-6t+4{t}^{2}+4+9{t}^{4} \\\\  & =15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302435 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "062642b3-def7-5feb-8f41-08b7e4a64ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299962} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd64be2-30aa-5f51-a354-0c648f752da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300175} {:answer/id #uuid "73e23c91-17b0-5276-ba29-6df6883eb88f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300538} {:answer/id #uuid "c02fe4ca-cc73-5724-8dbb-64c1e0b63d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300925} {:answer/id #uuid "e88569b0-7f63-5ac6-b787-2020ea0b2e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73e23c91-17b0-5276-ba29-6df6883eb88f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300538} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f006c5-3411-58f0-9d06-d677c36cb1c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301906}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "829808f0-e345-5eeb-99ad-5982ddad6fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32837" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{f}(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({t}^{2}-2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+4{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$, evaluate $({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(t)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+4\\cdot 2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+8t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ {\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}+8\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =6t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}+8\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{'}(0) & ={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(0)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(0)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(0)\\cdot {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(0) \\\\  & =(6(0)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+8\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (({0}^{3}-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({0}^{2}-2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+4(0)^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})+(3(0)^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2(0)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+8(0)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (3(0)^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2(0)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+8(0)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =(2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+8\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (-\\mathbf{i}-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =0(-1)+2(-2)+(0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b7a747-95ef-5439-8a0d-a5d0bc972bf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305178} {:answer/id #uuid "071d818f-582a-511b-8e1a-da0e02e5e527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305217} {:answer/id #uuid "39c46305-4821-5d35-b86b-257d73a82b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305701} {:answer/id #uuid "60474004-6f0b-518e-bd0a-d1fd73598741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306080} {:answer/id #uuid "79db6f46-1f9b-5903-82ac-d8484423c92c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60474004-6f0b-518e-bd0a-d1fd73598741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306080} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7db7aa7-b12e-53b6-82a4-b2d5f20ca566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308196}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a9de11b-dc85-5ae6-9285-a0d6cc055460" :question/math-academy-id "q-33336" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\operatorname{ln}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+1\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k} \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =1\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t) & ={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\cdot {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\operatorname{ln}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})+(\\operatorname{ln}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (\\mathbf{i}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{1}{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot t-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}t)+(\\operatorname{ln}t\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{t}\\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right)+t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}t+\\operatorname{ln}t-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}t+2-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df4d9e4-5aab-5758-b6bf-f561a4a5bc13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} {:answer/id #uuid "567f9cec-a4ac-5823-9ae9-ff55dac8a4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305989} {:answer/id #uuid "858bfa6f-4a26-5ea8-bf05-c82787e1d16e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306424} {:answer/id #uuid "db9b03e9-0749-562a-b299-e3af23995ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{2}^{t},\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307187} {:answer/id #uuid "f30b8be4-1b5a-550e-a1eb-f3bf87eff617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df4d9e4-5aab-5758-b6bf-f561a4a5bc13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} :answer-field/id #uuid "843487b0-a154-5051-ab18-86349bd94dcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "360e7d39-e582-5724-9fad-4481a2f3b45b" :question/math-academy-id "q-33446" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}$ given that  $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨{2}^{t},\\hspace{0.222em}{2}^{t+1},\\hspace{0.222em}{2}^{2t}+1⟩$ and $v(t)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}=v(t){\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)+{v}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t+1}),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{2t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}2,\\hspace{0.222em}{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}2,\\hspace{0.222em}2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}2⟩ \\\\ {v}^{'}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}\\right)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'} & =v(t){\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)+{v}^{'}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}2,\\hspace{0.222em}{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}2,\\hspace{0.222em}2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}2⟩-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t},\\hspace{0.222em}{2}^{t+1},\\hspace{0.222em}{2}^{2t}+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}}⟩-⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{{2}^{t+1}2\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{({2}^{2t}+1)\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}2}{{2}^{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ec8602-0288-50f5-9393-d24f3e9978eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{6},\\,{t}^{5}+4{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387973} {:answer/id #uuid "059c4a79-58ba-5ab8-812b-f1ffa1abcd8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{6}-5,\\,4{t}^{5}+2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387974} {:answer/id #uuid "22face6d-6d51-591d-a1b9-744a0e476e64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{t}^{6}+1,\\,4{t}^{5},\\,{t}^{3}-5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387975} {:answer/id #uuid "8428706c-8f90-591b-9287-63282825708a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387976} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb7b979-4cab-5af0-b6ed-092b5e887c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7{t}^{6},\\,6{t}^{5}-5,\\,4{t}^{3}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8428706c-8f90-591b-9287-63282825708a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387976} :answer-field/id #uuid "658bfb28-3b3a-5fa6-937f-fc8138b0b72f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387972}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c21f1368-688b-50ed-bde8-7422d801bdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-128896" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =⟨t,\\hspace{0.167em}5,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{4}⟩, \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{3},\\hspace{0.167em}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.167em}0,\\hspace{0.167em}4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3} & t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3}\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\hspace{0.167em}4{t}^{5}-t,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{3}⟩, \\\\ \\mathbf{f}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ t & 5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}t & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}t & 5 \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\hspace{0.167em}2{t}^{5}-t,\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t) & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\hspace{0.167em}4{t}^{5}-t,\\hspace{0.167em}{t}^{3}⟩+⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\hspace{0.167em}2{t}^{5}-t,\\hspace{0.167em}3{t}^{3}-10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\hspace{0.167em}6{t}^{5}-2t,\\hspace{0.167em}4{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9f86cd3-7815-52c3-a642-88091b5dca5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20t-2,\\,36{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390739} {:answer/id #uuid "3f10ad58-86c7-5488-87e8-2405ac572b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8t-2,\\,-48{t}^{2}+12t,\\,36{t}^{3}-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390740} {:answer/id #uuid "b218608b-b05e-57e2-a7b7-ae74abf570fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨48t-2,\\,-362{t}^{2}+12t,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390741} {:answer/id #uuid "a3285904-7a37-5bb0-9e4b-ea28118d456b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-28t,\\,-24{t}^{2},\\,36{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390742} {:answer/id #uuid "df14411c-6285-5ce6-9d91-f5503ce280c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-20t-2,\\,-72{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df14411c-6285-5ce6-9d91-f5503ce280c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-20t-2,\\,-72{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390743} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6adfc3-be4a-5dfa-b9ef-e4320cc373e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390738}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c0ab63c-e0ff-5937-9e2f-94c308127204" :question/math-academy-id "q-32347" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =⟨6{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}2t,\\hspace{0.222em}6⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨3,\\hspace{0.222em}3{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}4t-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12t,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}6t,\\hspace{0.222em}4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 12t & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3{t}^{2} & (4t-1)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & (4t-1)\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}12t & 0 \\\\ 3 & (4t-1)\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}12t & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨8t-2,\\hspace{0.222em}12t-48{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}36{t}^{3}-6⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{f}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 6{t}^{2} & 2t & 6 \\\\ 0 & 6t & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2t & 6 \\\\ 6t & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}6{t}^{2} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}6{t}^{2} & 2t \\\\ 0 & 6t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨-28t,\\hspace{0.222em}-24{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}36{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t) & =⟨8t-2,\\hspace{0.222em}12t-48{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}36{t}^{3}-6⟩+⟨-28t,\\hspace{0.222em}-24{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}36{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20t-2,\\hspace{0.222em}-72{t}^{2}+12t,\\hspace{0.222em}72{t}^{3}-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5e5d9ac-8a14-5201-9516-829a7b45050d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+8{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390800} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea13000-9bcb-54fe-a381-f6223d0bb92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390801} {:answer/id #uuid "37229cb1-9b3d-541c-ad4c-f9ff6d2bee90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390802} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f3c695-f3a3-58d0-9e05-5aa5b210d1ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2+2t\\,,\\,-6t+8{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390803} {:answer/id #uuid "2452df56-9f06-5ed0-821f-9ea53a5fecf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37229cb1-9b3d-541c-ad4c-f9ff6d2bee90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390802} :answer-field/id #uuid "b00615b6-9721-5844-9bad-568a5f743f33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390799}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d806e973-4767-5c33-a683-2e2483aec09e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32836" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨1-{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}1-{t}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}1-t⟩$, find $({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\times \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\times \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t)={\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\times \\mathbf{f}(t)+{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}-3{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}-1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2t)\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}-6t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0⟩\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{f}}^{''}(t)\\times \\mathbf{f}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ -2 & -6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-t\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -6t \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3}\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2-2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t)\\times {\\mathbf{f}}^{'}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}-2t & -1 \\\\ -2t & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}-2t & -3{t}^{2} \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨0\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0⟩\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}({\\mathbf{f}}^{'}\\times \\mathbf{f})^{'}(t) & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2-2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩+⟨0\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}2-2t\\hspace{0.167em},\\hspace{0.167em}-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3353c5-25db-5e97-9920-7001bdae531f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723510} {:answer/id #uuid "66414d4f-9055-51b9-b658-bbd4a383bc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723514} {:answer/id #uuid "66de178e-45de-5414-a820-934d7814840b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723515} {:answer/id #uuid "d3146e6d-b03b-53dd-8cf8-05dbacf0f873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723533} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd77ec6-234f-5fde-8364-1d6bba8f35b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddd77ec6-234f-5fde-8364-1d6bba8f35b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723534} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ebe4e57-e99b-5bf9-bf1f-2926df70ece0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723519}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "007622f5-6ac1-58be-a7f1-e283e4ad64d5" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=(- t^{3} - 1)\\,i+(3 t^{2} + 3)\\,j+t^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- t^{3} - 1)=- 3 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2} + 3)=6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})=2 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =- 3 t^{2}\\,i+6 t\\,j+2 t\\,k \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t^{2})=- 6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t)=6 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =- 6 t\\,i+6\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(0)(-1)+(6)(3)+(2)(0) \\\\  & =18 \\\\ P_2 & =(0)(0)+(0)(0)+(0)(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(0) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a28a204-0450-5f5c-9198-1dc31250c07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 t^{3} + 4 t^{2} - 7 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723517} {:answer/id #uuid "9915a58e-2d48-5915-b557-79380a9e9bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t^{3} + t^{2} - 4 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723520} {:answer/id #uuid "be378b94-d574-5e84-8721-1aa15a6f1457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 6 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723528} {:answer/id #uuid "c30fe383-bb93-511b-bd16-f84f3cb024cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t^{3} - t^{2} + 4 t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723529} {:answer/id #uuid "f5696126-d9c4-5849-ad09-e81b30fa674f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{3} + t^{2} - t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be378b94-d574-5e84-8721-1aa15a6f1457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 6 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723528} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac01c14b-740b-55de-95b4-9c89c5517e26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723524}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e115102-0aa3-579c-8fe1-b0154b41a4be" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(t - 2)\\,i- 2 t\\,j+t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(t^{2} + t)\\,i+t\\,j+t^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot g^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 2)=1 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 2 t)=-2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =\\,i-2\\,j+\\,k \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2} + t)=2 t + 1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})=3 t^{2} \\\\ g^{\\prime}(t) & =(2 t + 1)\\,i+\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(1)(t^{2} + t)+(-2)(t)+(1)(t^{3}) \\\\  & =t^{3} + t^{2} - t \\\\ P_2 & =(t - 2)(2 t + 1)+(- 2 t)(1)+(t)(3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =3 t^{3} + 2 t^{2} - 5 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =4 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 6 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c8d4d0-6598-58f1-b0e2-9d51af707ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\ln{(t )}}{2} + 6 + \\frac{6}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723507} {:answer/id #uuid "67bfc169-3d7a-5954-b380-7472539fb5e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 - 15 \\ln{(t )}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723516} {:answer/id #uuid "a0958627-c4d0-577f-b94a-1d5d64b7cdde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 21 \\ln{(t )} + 24 + \\frac{4}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723523} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b649e8-d4c8-5754-b06a-0719d726ffc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t} - \\frac{4}{t^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723530} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf32613-c394-5977-8423-7a9d69bda73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\ln{(t )} + 3 + \\frac{8}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcf32613-c394-5977-8423-7a9d69bda73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\ln{(t )} + 3 + \\frac{8}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723539} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb3c891-1037-51e5-ae4a-de9fe646e4d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5998b21e-5a65-5da2-b4a5-40c888949f7f" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =- 3 \\ln{(t )}\\,i- 2 t\\,j+\\frac{2}{t}\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =- 3 t\\,i+3 \\ln{(t )}\\,j- \\frac{2}{t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$ Assume $t>0$." :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot g^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 \\ln{(t )})=- \\frac{3}{t} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 2 t)=-2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right)=- \\frac{2}{t^{2}} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =- \\frac{3}{t}\\,i-2\\,j- \\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\,k \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t)=-3 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 \\ln{(t )})=\\frac{3}{t} \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t}\\right)=\\frac{2}{t^{2}} \\\\ g^{\\prime}(t) & =-3\\,i+\\frac{3}{t}\\,j+\\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\left(- \\frac{3}{t}\\right)(- 3 t)+(-2)(3 \\ln{(t )})+\\left(- \\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\right)\\left(- \\frac{2}{t}\\right) \\\\  & =- 6 \\ln{(t )} + 9 + \\frac{4}{t^{3}} \\\\ P_2 & =(- 3 \\ln{(t )})(-3)+(- 2 t)\\left(\\frac{3}{t}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =9 \\ln{(t )} - 6 + \\frac{4}{t^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =3 \\ln{(t )} + 3 + \\frac{8}{t^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db647fc-327e-5438-b8f1-599f7685c3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 54 t + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723508} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d5c244-c736-567a-8cff-ec98d19481b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27 t^{4} + 108 t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723526} {:answer/id #uuid "b5407feb-7290-5232-8611-9aeb0eeb2889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{135 t^{4}}{2} - 12 t^{2} - 27 t - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723527} {:answer/id #uuid "d08b7560-3aa2-5cfe-b8eb-cf6d655e7261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} - 54 t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723532} {:answer/id #uuid "de5d6480-5898-5c9a-b2f6-37b2d1c04a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "189 t^{4} + 32 t^{2} + 108 t + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db647fc-327e-5438-b8f1-599f7685c3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 54 t + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723508} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1591793-1f91-504a-b535-36ad122cf043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723525}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fb23ec1-6e13-5a4a-bb47-de87e3f76c31" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨3 t^{3} + 3,\\,2 t,\\,2 t^{2} + 1⟩$, find $(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{3} + 3)=9 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2} + 1)=4 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨9 t^{2},\\,2,\\,4 t⟩ \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(9 t^{2})=18 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(4 t)=4 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =⟨18 t,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(18 t)(3 t^{3} + 3)+(0)(2 t)+(4)(2 t^{2} + 1) \\\\  & =54 t^{4} + 8 t^{2} + 54 t + 4 \\\\ P_2 & =(9 t^{2})(9 t^{2})+(2)(2)+(4 t)(4 t) \\\\  & =81 t^{4} + 16 t^{2} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =135 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 54 t + 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d7a9b0-ba6a-505f-b59f-c84934a2c22a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 54 t^{2} - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723506} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9a292f-3140-5dbf-b551-d106374550ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162 t^{3} + 36 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723512} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe53a65-6f99-5361-b740-0bdb2edeb6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81 t^{4} + 36 t^{2} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723531} {:answer/id #uuid "eaad29fe-f20e-5277-b2d4-e86403f7c23d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 270 t^{4} - 108 t^{2} + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723536} {:answer/id #uuid "f2cb46ac-0c6c-573b-934d-92ac75107f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 27 t^{4} - 18 t^{2} - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09d7a9b0-ba6a-505f-b59f-c84934a2c22a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 54 t^{2} - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723506} :answer-field/id #uuid "4579a44b-0d5e-5193-a25f-3421dfe80149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723511}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c1ef875-08ca-5c88-b962-6b2e6956080e" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=- 3 t^{3}\\,i+(3 t^{2} - 2)\\,j+2 t\\,k$, find $(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t^{3})=- 9 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2} - 2)=6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =- 9 t^{2}\\,i+6 t\\,j+2\\,k \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 9 t^{2})=- 18 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t)=6 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =- 18 t\\,i+6\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(- 18 t)(- 3 t^{3})+(6)(3 t^{2} - 2)+(0)(2 t) \\\\  & =54 t^{4} + 18 t^{2} - 12 \\\\ P_2 & =(- 9 t^{2})(- 9 t^{2})+(6 t)(6 t)+(2)(2) \\\\  & =81 t^{4} + 36 t^{2} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =135 t^{4} + 54 t^{2} - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4db2b3-e025-5f86-a8c1-bc0a73c35260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t,\\,54 t^{2},\\,-18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723544} {:answer/id #uuid "8df4a47f-a6cb-55a9-898d-1c779c8071ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,0,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723547} {:answer/id #uuid "bce9f74a-e285-562e-9dad-462de73c0bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723550} {:answer/id #uuid "efa0f20f-ae68-5df5-a55e-e5c45eaa7b70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,18 t^{3} - 9 t + 9,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723552} {:answer/id #uuid "fad4f7a8-bb45-5ce8-bca3-9a113570021c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,72 t^{3} - 36 t + 36,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bce9f74a-e285-562e-9dad-462de73c0bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723550} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d54dfca-d4a3-53bf-970a-33dd4fd84dba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723543}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9816a80a-26f7-5ab7-b297-c498df4dd904" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨3 t^{2} - 1,\\,- 3 t - 3,\\,3 t^{3} - 3⟩$, find $(f^{\\prime}\\times f)^{\\prime}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the cross product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\times f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\times f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\times f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2} - 1)=6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t - 3)=-3 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{3} - 3)=9 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨6 t,\\,-3,\\,9 t^{2}⟩ \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t)=6 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(-3)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(9 t^{2})=18 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =⟨6,\\,0,\\,18 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 0 & 18 t \\\\ 3 t^{2} - 1 & - 3 t - 3 & 3 t^{3} - 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{1,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 18 t \\\\ - 3 t - 3 & 3 t^{3} - 3\\end{vmatrix}=54 t^{2} + 54 t \\\\ P_{1,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 18 t \\\\ 3 t^{2} - 1 & 3 t^{3} - 3\\end{vmatrix}=36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18 \\\\ P_{1,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 3 t^{2} - 1 & - 3 t - 3\\end{vmatrix}=- 18 t - 18 \\\\ P_1 & =⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩ \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6 t & -3 & 9 t^{2} \\\\ 6 t & -3 & 9 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{2,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 9 t^{2} \\\\ -3 & 9 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_{2,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}6 t & 9 t^{2} \\\\ 6 t & 9 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_{2,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 t & -3 \\\\ 6 t & -3\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_2 & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\times f)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f17d1d-8cf8-5453-80ea-fbe416dc37b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 24 t^{3} - 2 t - 1 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723541} {:answer/id #uuid "0dbd55d7-a479-5387-a5e0-2f3161f3c66c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 48 t^{3} - 4 t - 2 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723542} {:answer/id #uuid "8360a287-0b05-53ca-89e7-37a5daa77a7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - t - 5 \\\\ 4 - 35 t \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723546} {:answer/id #uuid "b06e9db5-3071-5050-b9c4-458e1f4ec6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 36 t^{3} - 3 t - 3 \\\\ 4 - 33 t \\\\ - 8 t^{2} - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723549} {:answer/id #uuid "f37ec804-ae53-5709-b7fe-c2f9b03f8f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 18 t^{3} - \\frac{3 t}{2} - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 - \\frac{33 t}{2} \\\\ - 4 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03f17d1d-8cf8-5453-80ea-fbe416dc37b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 24 t^{3} - 2 t - 1 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723541} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b0c43f-8b5a-51cc-acab-2a83c6fc3b0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723545}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c129f4fb-82d5-5476-8c23-145c24dded8c" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 t^{2} \\\\ t + 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ g(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ t - 1 \\\\ - 3 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the cross product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times g^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(-3)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2})=4 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t + 2)=1 \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 1)=1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t^{2})=- 6 t \\\\ g^{\\prime}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ - 6 t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 4 t & 1 \\\\ t & t - 1 & - 3 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{1,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 t & 1 \\\\ t - 1 & - 3 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=- 12 t^{3} - t + 1 \\\\ P_{1,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ t & - 3 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=t \\\\ P_{1,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 t \\\\ t & t - 1\\end{vmatrix}=- 4 t^{2} \\\\ P_1 & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - t + 1 \\\\ t \\\\ - 4 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 t^{2} & t + 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & - 6 t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{2,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 t^{2} & t + 2 \\\\ 1 & - 6 t\\end{vmatrix}=- 12 t^{3} - t - 2 \\\\ P_{2,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & t + 2 \\\\ 1 & - 6 t\\end{vmatrix}=2 - 17 t \\\\ P_{2,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 t^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=- 2 t^{2} - 3 \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - t - 2 \\\\ 2 - 17 t \\\\ - 2 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 24 t^{3} - 2 t - 1 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b0e6f3a-a6f5-5a5b-8736-75504782a6db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,- 2 e^{4 t},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723556} {:answer/id #uuid "3da10f2d-2c58-5a1d-8caa-29f707c0a7ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,- e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723557} {:answer/id #uuid "4a242423-8170-50dc-a558-0b9e7914f40b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,2 e^{2 t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723558} {:answer/id #uuid "624d1e86-69a4-5774-a6d3-0bfdbf966bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723559} {:answer/id #uuid "8766f12a-a624-5bba-bf10-8af18c52195e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,e^{2 t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a242423-8170-50dc-a558-0b9e7914f40b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,2 e^{2 t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723558} :answer-field/id #uuid "856534c6-7179-5f48-b48e-329c9b3017b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723560}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dc45519-249e-53bf-ad66-0c4633428e6f" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{\\prime}$ given that $f(t)=⟨e^{- t},\\,e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩$ and $v(t)=e^{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{\\prime}=v(t)f^{\\prime}(t)+v^{\\prime}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{- t})=- e^{- t} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{3 t})=3 e^{3 t} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{t + 3})=e^{t + 3} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨- e^{- t},\\,3 e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\ v^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{t})=e^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(e^{t})⟨- e^{- t},\\,3 e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,3 e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\ P_2 & =(e^{t})⟨e^{- t},\\,e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{\\prime} & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,2 e^{2 t + 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}]}
